// A bare `x := asm { … -> T }` binding (not a direct `return asm`) types
// correctly: the value output flows through the local and out as the exit
// code. Without the `inferType` `.asm_expr` arm the binding infers
// `.unresolved` and silently produces 0. aarch64-pinned
// via `.build` → runs on a matching host, ir-only elsewhere.
main :: () -> i64 {
    x := asm { "mov %[out], #99", [out] "=r" -> i64 };
    return x;
}
